`LICENSE` holds the verbatim Apache-2.0 text and nothing else, so that licence
detection tools recognise the repository as Apache-2.0. This file carries the
copyright line, the SPDX identifier and the scope notes.

Scope
-----
- Apache-2.0 covers this project's own source code (the repository and the
  `nmrforge` package). It does not change the terms of any third-party component,
  and it is not the licence of the files under
  packaging/linux/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/.
- LGPL is used only where a *packaged distribution* actually bundles an
  LGPL-covered library: the Linux AppImage ships Qt/PySide6, whose licence option
  in use is LGPL-3.0-only. For that binary the LGPL obligations apply to those
  libraries (and to the relink/replace route), not to this project's source. The
  texts and notices travel inside the AppImage
  (packaging/linux/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/), are printable with
  `nmrforge --licenses`, and the build script accepts self-built bindings
  (PYSIDE6_REQUIREMENT / SHIBOKEN6_REQUIREMENT / EXTRA_PIP_ARGS) so a recipient
  can replace or relink them.
- Third-party components keep their own licences; see THIRD_PARTY.md.
- The reasoning behind the source/binary licence split is in LICENSE_OPTIONS.md.
